WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.730
Belle Starr has come down through time as
one of the great anti-heroines of the Old

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.730
West.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:09.580
She is the Bandit Queen, the female Robin
Hood, who was quick with her fists and even

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.480
quicker with her Colt 45.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.620
The reality was quite different.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.610
The Belle of history was a battler who made
some bad choices in men, ended up twice widowed

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:23.330
with two children and made the most of the
cards she was dealt – only to meet the most

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.890
violent of ends.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:34.070
In today’s Biographics, we go beyond the
legend to reveal the real Belle Starr.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:45.149
Formative Years
Myra Maybelle Shirley, the future Belle Starr,

00:00:45.149 --> 00:00:49.680
was born on February 5th, 1848 in Jasper County,
Southwest Missouri.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.420
With that fact established, drilling down
on the rest of her life becomes far less certain.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.340
Much of what is accepted is the stuff of dime
novel fiction.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:02.340
Sorting out the fact from fiction is a major
challenge.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.819
We do know that her father, John Shirley was
onto his third wife when Myra came along.

00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:12.920
That third wife was named Eliza Pennington
Hatfield, a member of the Hatfield family

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.859
who famously feuded with the McCoy’s.

00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:20.689
The couple had three other children, all boys,
with Myra being the second oldest.

00:01:20.689 --> 00:01:24.079
John Shirley was a wheat, corn and hog farmer.

00:01:24.079 --> 00:01:29.420
When Myra was six years of age, he sold the
farm for a tidy profit and relocated the family

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.919
to Carthage, Missouri.

00:01:30.919 --> 00:01:35.310
He invested in real estate, managing to take
possession of an entire city block that housed

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:39.209
a livery stable, blacksmith shop, tavern and
hotel.

00:01:39.209 --> 00:01:43.489
John Shirley was a slave owner who was ardently
pro-slavery.

00:01:43.489 --> 00:01:48.259
In the explosive years before the Civil War,
tensions were high between pro and anti-slavery

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:50.039
forces in Missouri.

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:54.450
When his oldest son, Bud, joined an infamous
gang of Confederate sympathizers known as

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:58.059
Quantrill’s Raiders, John was extremely
proud.

00:01:58.059 --> 00:02:02.659
Meanwhile, Myra, who insisted that she be
called Belle, was growing into a fine young

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:03.659
lady.

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:07.229
Her parents were among the most prominent
in Carthage and she was able to enjoy a life

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:08.539
of semi-privilege.

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:12.370
She attended the Carthage Female Academy,
doing well in her studies, where she studied

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.700
languages, mathematics and grammar.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.910
She was also a talented piano player who would
entertain guests in the lobby of the family

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:19.910
owned hotel.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:24.280
When he was home from his raiding expeditions,
Belle’s older brother Bud taught her to

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.280
shoot.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.319
She became an excellent shot, developing a
reputation as a markswoman that would later

00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:32.599
fuel her reputation as the bandit queen.

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:35.049
Belle was 13 when the Civil War erupted.

00:02:35.049 --> 00:02:39.680
Carthage found itself as a central point of
hostilities, with no fewer than 13 battles

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.870
being waged in the surrounding area during
the four years of the conflict.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.560
With the war right on their doorstep, every
person in Carthage was forced to choose sides.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:53.920
Pro and anti-Confederacy factions developed
with tensions escalating by the day.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.540
It has been reported that the teenaged Belle
acted as a spy for the Confederacy and even

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:01.180
that she joined Quantrill’s Raiders.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.359
Both suggestions are unlikely.

00:03:03.359 --> 00:03:06.799
However, any news that she may have gotten
about Union troop movements she would have

00:03:06.799 --> 00:03:08.459
no doubt passed on to Bud.

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:13.629
In June, 1864, Bud was shot and killed by
Union soldiers in Sarcoxie, Missouri when

00:03:13.629 --> 00:03:15.469
they surrounded the house he was owned by
a Confederate sympathizer.

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:20.329
Desperate to prevent further tragedy, the
family packed up and moved to Texas.

00:03:20.329 --> 00:03:22.330
They had gotten out of Carthage just in time.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:26.139
Three months later it was burned to the ground
by Confederate rebels, determined to drive

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.969
Union soldiers from the town.

00:03:27.969 --> 00:03:31.470
Belle drove one of the family’s wagons as
they wound their way down from Missouri to

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.930
a small town ten miles south-east of Dallas
called Scyene.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.959
Things didn’t go nearly as well for the
Shirley’s in Texas as it had in Missouri.

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:43.580
John had hoped to reinvest in a hotel but
those plans didn’t work out and he was forced

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.999
to return to farming.

00:03:44.999 --> 00:03:49.080
Conflict arose with the locals who accused
John of taking more than his share of water

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.269
from the communal well.

00:03:50.269 --> 00:03:52.560
Belle was enrolled at the local one-room schoolhouse.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.139
Her attendance, however, was erratic.

00:03:55.139 --> 00:03:58.550
This was probably because she was bored with
the material, having already covered it at

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.740
the girl’s school in Carthage.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:07.560
Marriage
While back in Carthage, Belle had come across

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.690
a boy by the name of John Reed.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:14.639
Reed, who was two years older than Belle,
joined Quantrill’s Raiders when he was 17.

00:04:14.639 --> 00:04:19.630
He was tall and stocky and his ability with
his fists and with a gun earned him the respect

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.060
of the older members of the gang.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:25.690
Belle admired him from afar but her family
moved away before a relationship could develop.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:30.150
Belle was ecstatic to learn, sometime around
1865, that the Reed’s had also relocated

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.150
to Texas.

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:35.490
They quickly became a couple and, on November
1, 1866 they were married.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.250
Belle was eighteen at the time.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:41.920
Jim and Belle moved in with the Shirley family,
where Jim helped out on the family farm.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.419
Jim didn’t take to farm work and tried his
hand as a salesman.

00:04:45.419 --> 00:04:49.270
He worked for a saddle maker in Dallas, selling
saddles and bridles for a time.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:52.810
By the end of 1867, however, Jim’s family
had moved back to Missouri.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.930
He and Belle decided to join them.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:58.120
The Reed’s set themselves up on a farm in
Bates County.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.169
Jim worked the land with his brothers.

00:05:00.169 --> 00:05:03.990
Then, in September, 1868, Belle gave birth
to a daughter, Rosie Lee.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.169
From the start Belle took to calling the baby
‘her little pearl’.

00:05:07.169 --> 00:05:09.430
Soon everyone was calling the baby Pearl.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:13.449
The first opportunity that John and Eliza
Shirley had to see their grand-daughter was

00:05:13.449 --> 00:05:17.460
when Belle returned to Texas to attend the
funeral of her younger brother Ed.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.560
The events surrounding the murder are cloudy,
but it appears that he was involved in horse

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:22.560
theft.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:26.230
Following the funeral and reunion with her
parents, Belle returned to the Reed farm in

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:27.230
Missouri.

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:31.879
Her relationship with Jim was strained, as
he spent less and less time on the farm and

00:05:31.879 --> 00:05:33.789
more at the horse racing track.

00:05:33.789 --> 00:05:37.800
It was while at the races that Jim ran into
a man named Tom Starr.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:42.100
Starr was a half Cherokee outlaw who made
a living by selling whiskey in Indian territory,

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.830
a practice which happened to be a Federal
crime.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:48.569
Starr ran the enterprise with his sons and
they were soon joined by Jim Reed.

00:05:48.569 --> 00:05:53.330
Jim’s foray into the outlaw world escalated
dramatically when his brother, Scott, was

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.330
murdered.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:58.620
Jim vowed revenge and hunted down the killer,
dispatching both him and his brother.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:02.409
Belle now found herself with a husband who
was being hunted by, not just the law, but

00:06:02.409 --> 00:06:03.659
also the friends of the men he had killed.

00:06:03.659 --> 00:06:04.659
Jim knew he had to get out of Missouri, so
he relocated his young family to Los Angeles.

00:06:04.659 --> 00:06:08.210
We don’t know what he did there to support
the family, but suspicions are strong that

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:12.460
it was through such nefarious means as stage
coach robbery and gambling.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:17.750
On February 22nd, 1871, Belle gave birth to
a second child – a boy who was named James

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.639
Edwin, nicknamed Eddie.

00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:23.300
Only a month later, Jim was accused of involvement
in a counterfeit money scam and was forced

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.159
again to relocate his family.

00:06:25.159 --> 00:06:28.180
When the L.A. authorities began looking into
his case, they discovered that he was also

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:29.180
wanted for murder.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:32.389
Jim skipped town and made his way on horseback
to Texas.

00:06:32.389 --> 00:06:35.530
Belle and the two children took the stagecoach.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:41.040
In March, 1871, Belle turned up at the family
farm in Texas with two kids and a wanted husband.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:45.050
Belle’s father helped them to set up on
a small farm near Coon Creek in Bosque County.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.870
But Jim Reed had already proven that he was
no farmer.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:51.950
Soon the farm was attracting a regular assortment
of vagabonds, who would sit around with Jim

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:54.120
and plan out their various crimes.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.840
Jim became involved in rustling livestock.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:01.340
When he learned that a local man by the name
of Dick Cravey had $4,000 in cash stashed

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:04.720
at his house, Jim and his brother, Sol, couldn’t
resist the temptation.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:08.230
However, the robbery was botched and they
ended up murdering Cravey.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:11.259
A few months later the brothers were accused
of murdering another man.

00:07:11.259 --> 00:07:14.669
This man, whose last name was Wheeler, had
apparently reported to the authorities what

00:07:14.669 --> 00:07:17.340
he knew about the Reed mob’s illegal activities.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.789
He was found with his tongue cut out.

00:07:19.789 --> 00:07:25.490
This latest outrage resulted in both Jim and
Sol having a $500 reward placed on their capture,

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:26.970
dead or alive.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:29.000
It was time to move once again.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:33.050
Leaving the children with Belle’s parents,
the couple headed into Choctaw Indian territory,

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.539
where the authorities would be unable to follow.

00:07:35.539 --> 00:07:37.450
Jim was unable to stay out of trouble.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:42.500
On November 19, 1873, along with two accomplices,
he rode to the farm of a wealthy retired judge

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:44.590
who lived near the South Canadian River.

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:49.050
The judge and his wife were hung from a tree
and forced to divulge the location of cash

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:50.090
in the house.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:54.660
The bandits got away with the huge sum of
$30,000.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.310
By now the strain on the marriage was too
much.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:01.100
Belle was fed up with the life of crime that
her husband had forced her into.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:04.840
She packed up and took the children back to
the family farm in Scyene.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:08.970
Reed headed for San Antonio, where he took
up with a woman named Rosa McCommas.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:13.520
He continued his outlaw ways but fate caught
up with him when a former associate shot him

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:19.410
in the back on August 6th, 1874.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:25.300
Belle Starr
Belle was now a widow with two young children

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.300
to care for.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.430
She stayed on the family with her parents.

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:30.960
In 1876, John Shirley died.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:34.060
This forced Eliza to sell the farm and relocate
to Dallas.

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:36.340
Belle and the children went with her.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:40.530
Allegedly, Belle was briefly married for three
weeks to Charles Younger, uncle of Cole Younger

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:44.750
in 1878, but this is not substantiated by
any evidence.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:50.810
On June 5, 1880 Belle married Sam Starr the
son of her husband’s former associate Tom

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:53.300
Starr and settled in the Indian territory.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:57.760
There, she learned ways of organizing, planning
and fencing for the rustlers, horse thieves

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:00.910
and bootleggers, as well as harboring them
from the law.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:05.480
At twenty-three, the half-Cherokee Sam was
nine years younger than his new bride.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:10.420
They moved onto Cherokee Nation territory
and settled into a homestead some 760 miles

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:11.870
southwest of Fort Smith.

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.280
They cleared three acres of land and planted
corn.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.730
There were plenty of fish in the nearby river
and game was also plentiful.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:23.010
It seemed like the ideal existence and it
could have been if Belle’s past hadn’t

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:24.640
gotten in the way.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:29.320
Former associates of Jim Reed began to learn
that Belle had a hideout in Indian territory,

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:30.850
safe from the reach of the law.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:34.640
So many outlaws began turning up that Belle
and Saw were forced to convert a nearby cave

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.410
into a sort of robber’s roost with three
log cabins being erected.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:43.250
Up until now, Belle had managed to keep herself
from actual involvement in illegally activity.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:47.820
That changed in 1882 when she and Sam asked
a neighbor if they could put some horses in

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.141
his pen prior to their selling them.

00:09:49.141 --> 00:09:53.630
The neighbor agreed but, on inspection, pointed
out that at least two of the horses belonged

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:55.350
to other local farmers.

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:58.890
Sam and Belle ignored the claims and went
ahead and sold the horses.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:02.290
When the original owners of the stolen horses
found out, they pressed charges.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:06.820
Sam and Belle were handed an indictment to
appear before the court on the charge of larceny.

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:09.930
Sam’s father, Tom, put up bail for the couple.

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:12.430
Both Belle and Sam were found guilty.

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:16.300
Sam was given a year’s prison time in Detroit,
Michigan while Belle was sentenced to two

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:19.300
concurrent six-month spells at the same facility.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:22.990
With their mother and step-father in jail,
the children were farmed out to family and

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:23.990
friends.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:27.970
Sam and Belle were both model prisoners, earning
themselves an early release after nine months.

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:32.340
They settled back into life on the farm and
things were pretty quiet for a few months.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:37.470
Then, in December, 1884 a former associate
of Jim Reed by the name of Jim Middleton turned

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:40.340
up, looking for a place of refuge from the
law.

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:44.550
Middleton was wanted for murder and the law
was hot on his trail.

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:47.130
Middleton hung around the area for several
months.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:51.570
Then, one day, Belle and Sam’s ranch was
raided by law enforcement officers from Lamar

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:52.570
County.

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:55.770
The officers had received permission from
the Cherokee nation leaders to conduct the

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:56.770
raid.

00:10:56.770 --> 00:11:00.570
Middleton was not in residence at the time,
but the raid scared him enough to make him

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:01.720
want to make a run for it.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:05.570
But with the law so close on his trail, he
couldn’t figure out a way to get out the

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:07.470
area without being detected.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:11.420
Belle came to his rescue, suggesting that
she drive a wagon with the children in tow,

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.270
to visit relatives in Arkansas.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:17.610
Middleton would hide in the wagon covers and
make his getaway when they were clear of prying

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:18.610
eyes.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:22.670
The plan was working well and, after some
time, Middleton was ready to light out on

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:23.670
his own.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.500
However, seventeen-year-old Pearl refused
to let him take her horse.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:30.121
This led to fourteen-year old Eddie heading
off to the nearest farm in an attempt to buy

00:11:30.121 --> 00:11:31.121
a horse.

00:11:31.121 --> 00:11:33.610
He came back with a broken down, half-blind
mare.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:38.610
It was hardly the ideal getaway transport
but it was all that Middleton had and he set

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:42.470
out on his own, with Belle’s Colt 45 as
his only protection.

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:47.060
Five days later the horse was found in some
scrub on a riverbank, not far from Fort Smith.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:52.230
Then, on May 11th, Middleton’s body was
found a couple of hundred yards downstream.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:55.880
The authorities soon traced the gun that was
in his holster back to Belle.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:59.880
They also discovered that the horse, though
legitimately purchased by Eddie, had previously

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:00.880
been stolen.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.900
The end result was that Belle was once again
up on charges of larceny.

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:07.530
Belle was found not guilty this time around.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:11.000
However, she returned home only to discover
that her husband, Sam, had been wounded in

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.780
a shootout with Indian police.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:15.970
Sam had by now become ensconced in his own
life of crime.

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:19.960
Fearful of the rough justice that Indian police
were likely to dish out, Belle convinced him

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:22.710
to hand himself in to Federal authorities.

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:27.060
Sam was indicted for trial in February, 1887
and then released on bail.

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:31.190
On December 17th, Sam, Belle and the children
attended a party at a neighbor’s house.

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:35.460
Everything was laughter and merriment until
Frank West, the local law officer turned up.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:39.390
He and Sam got into an argument that soon
devolved into a gun battle.

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:45.040
Within minutes both men were dead.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:50.360
Family Problems
Belle Starr was now widowed for the second

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.360
time.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:54.310
Sam’s death made possession of the ranch
on Cherokee land a problem.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:57.920
They had not bought the land, it being in
their possession due to Sam’s Indian blood.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:01.110
Now that he was dead, however, Belle’s right
of possession was disputed.

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:05.440
With pressure mounting on her to get out of
Cherokee territory she decided there was another

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:06.440
solution.

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:10.100
She married Sam’s brother, Bill July, alias
Jim Starr.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:14.470
She was once again married to a Cherokee and
so, had possession rights to the land.

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:17.800
Now 39, Belle was fifteen years older than
her third husband.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:23.260
The marriage of convenience was not pleasing
to Pearl, aged nineteen, or Eddie, aged seventeen.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:28.260
Both of them constantly argued with Jim, which
was a source of ongoing frustration for Belle.

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:32.060
Around this time, Pearl fell in love with
a young man who, in the course of time, approached

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:35.050
Belle to ask her consent to marry her daughter.

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:38.990
Belle flatly refused, giving the reason that
she had long told Pearl that she could only

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:42.690
marry a man who had at least $25,000 worth
of property.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:46.410
She later tried to trick the young man by
sending him a letter with Pear’s forged

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:49.470
signature on it, stating that she had married
someone else.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:53.850
The young couple soon figured out the ruse
and continued to see one another behind Belle’s

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:54.850
back.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:56.130
Before long, Pearl became pregnant.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:14:01.220
Belle was not happy, giving her daughter two
options – have an abortion or never bring

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:03.130
the child into her presence.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:07.920
Pearl chose the latter option, giving birth
to a girl she called Flossie on April 22,

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:08.920
1887.

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:11.370
She took the baby to live with her paternal
grandparents.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:14.500
In 1887, Jim was arrested for horse theft.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:17.970
By this time, however, Belle was making an
effort to go straight.

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:20.980
She had stopped allowing fugitives to use
her place as a hideout.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:24.530
When it came time for Jim’s trial, she refused
to assist in his defense.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:27.340
Meanwhile, young Eddie Star was having his
own problems.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.770
He was shot while trying to steal a horse.

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:31.480
Belle feared that he would die.

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:35.011
She sent a message to Pearl, telling her that
she had better come back to see her brother

00:14:35.011 --> 00:14:36.110
for the last time.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:39.000
She added however, that she was not to bring
the baby.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.750
Pearl returned to see Eddie, who recovered
from his injury.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:45.690
Belle put pressure on her daughter to give
Flossie up for adoption during the visit.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:47.090
Pearl outrightly refused.

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:49.010
But Belle was a stubborn woman.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:53.390
She maneuvered things behind the scenes and
Flossie was taken from Pearl and placed in

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.640
an orphanage in November, 1888.

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:58.780
Eddie was now up on horse theft charges of
his own.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:01.050
Again, Belle refused to participate in the
defense.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:03.440
Eddie’s trial was scheduled for March 1889.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:07.050
He returned to the family homestead and, reportedly,
threatened to kill his mother.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:09.930
He then took off, never to see Belle again.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:13.850
Belle’s problems escalated when a couple,
the Watsons, turned up at the farm looking

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.250
for sharecropping work.

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:18.970
Belle decided to take them up on the offer,
keen to take in some extra money.

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:21.010
Belle became quite friendly with Mrs. Watson.

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:25.020
On one occasion the woman revealed that her
husband was wanted for murder.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:27.410
This caused warning bells in Belle’s mind.

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:31.650
If the Cherokee Tribal Council found out that
she was again harboring fugitives, they would

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:33.760
surely kick her off the land.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:38.100
Belle offered to give the Watsons, their sharecropping
fee back to get them to leave.

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:40.500
But Edgar Watson refused.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:45.060
It was only when Belle revealed that she knew
that Watson was a wanted man that he left,

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:49.540
taking up with his wife in a nearby tenant
cabin.

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:54.820
End of the Line

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:59.290
On July 2nd, 1889, Belle and her young husband,
Jim, left on horseback to meet Jim’s trial

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:00.650
appointment at Fort Smith.

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:05.360
Belle’s intention was to accompany him halfway,
pay a debt at a store on King’s Creek and

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:06.690
then return home.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.700
They stayed the night with friends some twenty
miles from Fort Smith.

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:13.300
The next morning, Belle turned for home while
Jim carried on to the fort.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:16.980
Belle stopped off at King’s Creek where
she had lunch at the local store.

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:20.490
Further along the trail she stopped at the
home of a man named Jackson Rowe.

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:24.890
This was a popular meeting place for locals.She
hoped to see her son Eddie, who had been staying

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:27.010
there, but he left before she arrived.

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:31.160
Present was Edgar Watson, the sharecropper
who Belle had forced off her land.

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.700
As he saw Belle arrive, he promptly left.

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:37.570
After a short time eating and conversing with
friends, Belle got back on her horse and continued

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:39.360
toward home.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:40.360
She never made it.

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:42.940
She was blasted from her horse by a shotgun
blast.

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:47.250
The killer then approached the dying figure
on the ground and blasted again.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.630
Belle’s panicked horse galloped for home.

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:52.240
A concerned Pearl set out to find her mother.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:56.160
By the time she got to the murder site, a
young boy had already found the body.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.640
Belle was taken to a farmhouse, barely alive.

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:04.059
Pearl was just in time to be alongside at
the moment that her mother took her last breath.

00:17:04.059 --> 00:17:08.439
The question of who killed Belle Starr has
intrigued historians for well over a century.

00:17:08.439 --> 00:17:12.640
Both of her children have been suspects, Eddie
had threatened his mother at least once after

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:16.929
she had disciplined him with a bullwhip, but
the most likely candidate is Edgar Watson.

00:17:16.929 --> 00:17:18.990
Watson was actually put on trial for the murder.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:22.379
However, the evidence was deemed as circumstantial
and he was acquitted.

00:17:22.379 --> 00:17:26.179
He eventually returned to Florida, where he
was killed in a shootout with a posse.

00:17:26.179 --> 00:17:30.040
No other efforts were made to track down the
killer of Belle Starr.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:33.980
There were several other potential suspects
besides Watson, including July himself.

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:37.559
Apparently July had been caught with a young
Cherokee girl, and Belle had been making his

00:17:37.559 --> 00:17:38.799
life hell.

00:17:38.799 --> 00:17:42.870
Just a few weeks after Belle’s death, July
was mortally wounded by a deputy who was on

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:43.870
his trail.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:49.779
The facts of Belle Starr’s life are certainly
not as exciting or outlandish as they fictionalized

00:17:49.779 --> 00:17:54.389
version that began with the dime novel Belle
Starr: The Bandit Queen or The Female Jesse

00:17:54.389 --> 00:17:56.559
James in 1889.

00:17:56.559 --> 00:18:01.120
In summarizing her life for a Fort Smith Elevator
reporter about a year before her death, Belle

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.970
said, ‘I regard myself as a woman who has
seen much of life.’

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:09.919
The reality was that she was not the female
Jesse James, she wasn’t even a bandit queen.

00:18:09.919 --> 00:18:16.370
What she was a twice widowed woman with two
children who did what she could to survive,

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:17.980
only to be shot down in cold blood.

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:22.879
Hers is a story of hardship and tragedy in
the real Old West.

00:18:22.879 --> 00:18:24.990
Her grave site is near Eufair Lake, Oklahoma.

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:28.919
A horse was engraved on her tombstone, along
with these words:

00:18:28.919 --> 00:18:33.820
Shed not for her the bitter tear,
Nor give the heart to vain regret

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:57.249
Tis but the casket that lies here,
The gem that filled it sparkles yet.

